[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657401785","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114013#issuecomment-3657401785","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114013","id":3657401785,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Z_4W5","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-15T20:12:21Z","updated_at":"2025-12-15T20:13:35Z","body":"This sounds like the correct behaviour. The camera marked as current is the camera used for rendering. The `XRCamera3D` node was purely introduced so positioning is controlled, but if you do not make it the current camera, its settings will not be used.\n\nIn this way you could have multiple XRCamera3D nodes with just one current, which is something we use in XR Tools for switching between loading environment and the active scene.\n\nThe `use-xr` property on the viewport tells the rendering system to get stereo camera data directly from the `XRInterface` and it overrides applicable settings for whatever camera node is currently in use.. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657401785/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658366369","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114013#issuecomment-3658366369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114013","id":3658366369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aDj2h","user":{"login":"EviTRea","id":32661913,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjYxOTEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32661913?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea","html_url":"https://github.com/EviTRea","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EviTRea/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T01:55:14Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T01:55:14Z","body":"> The camera marked as current is the camera used for rendering. The `XRCamera3D` node was purely introduced so positioning is controlled, but if you do not make it the current camera, its settings will not be used.\n\nWait, so...if I understand correctly, it wasn't the regular Camera3D overriding my XRCamera3D, it's actually the Camera3D got overrided by XR motion data...?\n\nXRCamera3D a